-- title:
--   Regular pair on a finite algebra over a local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring and let $B$ be a nonzero commutative ring which is an $A$-algebra and finite as an $A$-module. Let $a,b$ be elements of the maximal ideal of $A$. Assume that multiplication by the image of $a$ in $B$ is injective on $B$ (i.e. the image of $a$ is a non-zero-divisor on $B$), that the quotient ring $B/(a)$, where $(a)$ denotes the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $a$ under the structure map $A \to B$, is reduced, and that the class of the image of $b$ in $B/(a)$ lies in no minimal prime ideal of $B/(a)$. The conclusion is that the two-term list $[a,b]$ is a regular sequence on $B$ in the sense of Mathlib: the image of $a$ acts injectively on $B$, the image of $b$ acts injectively on the quotient $B/(a)$, and the ideal generated by $a$ and $b$ does not act on $B$ with full image, i.e. $(a,b)B \neq B$.
--
--   This is the standard criterion producing a length-two regular sequence on a finite algebra over a local ring from reducedness of the first quotient; it supplies the regular-sequence hypothesis of the miracle-flatness argument used to prove freeness, hence flatness, of finite covers of modular curves at a point. It is invoked in the flatness and local-freeness statements for the Deligne–Rapoport-type models and the Igusa scheme.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_RingTheory_Sequence_isRegular_pair_of_isSMulRegular_of_isReduced_of_forall_notMem_minimalPrimes.lean

